.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-POLICY-GET" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-policy-get - Show an on-demand port policy


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel policy get <policy> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Show one on-demand port policy: its target, access mode, state, ID and generation. Use the ID
and generation to update it with pb tunnel policy allow or end it with pb tunnel policy revoke.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for get

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel policy get pol_abc
  pb tunnel policy get pol_abc --json
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel-policy(1)\fP
